<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33918" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλῠμος</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλύω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>case, quiver</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a kind of Phrygian
				<i>pipe</i>, made of box-wood, with a horn tip and bend in the
			left pipe, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλυμοι αὐλοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					450
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				644
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.Com.
				18
			</span></i>; used by the Cyprians, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.Jun.
				3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλυμος, ἡ</span> (masc. in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i>), 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελίνη</span>
			, <i>millet</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				2.110
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				398
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.15.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				55.16
			</span></i> (Telmessus, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				12.3.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.98
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
